        "id": 1135107
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-13T22:12:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you sure it is the service? It\u0027s defined in BuildFlags.h depending on `BINDER_WITH_KERNEL_IPC` macro (so local to compilation unit / build target).",
      "parentUuid": "558e34ae_4e1e4a8f",
      "revId": "07117cd56349fd65ea7ddc2dd8a56167f011a664",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d3befc4_87ae8d9b",
        "filename": "libs/binder/tests/binderRpcTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1303,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-13T22:18:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes: `kEnableKernelIpc` marks whether the _client_ supports kernel IPC, and `noKernel` whether the _service_ supports it. The first one is set in `BuildFlags.h`, but is orthogonal to the second value.\n\nThe `noKernel` value determines which service binary the current test suite uses: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/libs/binder/tests/binderRpcTest.cpp;l\u003d266. If the chosen binary doesn\u0027t support the IPC tests, we disable them regardless of `kEnableKernelIpc`.",
      "parentUuid": "d3220e74_ed39b92b",
      "revId": "07117cd56349fd65ea7ddc2dd8a56167f011a664",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b11cfc24_6b860c60",
