        "id": 1135107
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-13T23:09:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I misread what you said. So we\u0027re testing non-IPC client connecting to IPC-enabled service, ok. And on Trusty you hardcoded this to only connect to non-IPC version.\n\nSo I need some way to configure which tests to run. Maybe `BINDER_TEST_KERNEL_IPC`. Ideally, there would be no hardcoded BINDER_RPC_TO_TRUSTY_TEST but a more flexible version that would be applicable to linux too.",
      "parentUuid": "0d3befc4_87ae8d9b",
      "revId": "07117cd56349fd65ea7ddc2dd8a56167f011a664",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
